{"basis" 2065 "lineage" "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1" "source" ":org/Math-Academy" "question" {:db/id 17592186402002 :question/id #uuid "1fb0889d-6fed-5243-aaf7-929089854f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31954" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186115250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4683baa-7e31-565a-90dd-81bc97617456" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402004} {:answer/id #uuid "e66e39bf-af21-54ee-9c01-1e665e79afcb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402005} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb3bda1-f364-5e06-b3f9-1ec1294cdafe" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402006} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae71a29-b56a-5e44-b3f7-481f0faef4bc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402007} {:answer/id #uuid "e81114b5-b5d4-5ed1-9aad-cfda69edeb8e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4683baa-7e31-565a-90dd-81bc97617456" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186402004} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce793d72-97c8-5680-9b23-e9cde7d661bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186402003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $D$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${D}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $D$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $D$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${D}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} "facts" [[17592186402002 "question/answer-fields" "17592186402003" 17592186045417] [17592186402002 "question/difficulty" "17592186045487" 17592186045417] [17592186402002 "question/id" "#uuid \"1fb0889d-6fed-5243-aaf7-929089854f2b\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402002 "question/math-academy-id" "\"q-31954\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402002 "question/problem" "\"The inverse of the $2\\\\times 2$ matrix $D$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${D}^{-1}.$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}[D\\\\,|\\\\,I] & =[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\\\text{___________} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\\\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\\\end{aligned}]\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402002 "question/worked-solution" "\"We write down $D$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $D$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}[D\\\\,|\\\\,I] & =[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\\\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\\\\\  & ∼[\\\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\\\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\\\end{aligned}]\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe matrix ${D}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \\n\\n$$\\n{D}^{-1}=[\\\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\\\\\ 2 & 1\\\\end{aligned}].\\n$$\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/choices" "17592186402004" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/choices" "17592186402005" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/choices" "17592186402006" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/choices" "17592186402007" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/choices" "17592186402008" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/correct" "17592186402004" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/id" "#uuid \"ce793d72-97c8-5680-9b23-e9cde7d661bb\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/key" "\"selection\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402003 "answer-field/type" "17592186045493" 17592186045417] [17592186402004 "answer/id" "#uuid \"d4683baa-7e31-565a-90dd-81bc97617456\"" 17592186045417] [17592186402004 "answer/type" "17592186045498" 17592186045417] [17592186402004 "answer/value" "\"{D}^{-1}=[\\\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\\\\\ 2 & -1\\\\end{aligned}]\"" 17592186045417]] "source_id" "q-31954" "judgment" {"status" "source_error" "reasoning" "The final operation is R_1:=R_1-R_2, giving right-hand rows (-1,1) and (2,-1). Thus option b is the inverse; multiplying it by D gives the identity matrix. MA's final augmented matrix agrees, but its concluding inverse formula incorrectly changes the bottom-right entry to +1. That formula is absent from the choices. The captured Correct grade does not identify the submitted choice and cannot resolve this internal source inconsistency." "confidence" 1 "answers" [{"key" "selection" "correct_value" "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "correct_option" "b" "value_type" "math" "wrong_value" "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "correct_keys" [] "wrong_keys" [] "ma_value" "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "ma_basis" "worked_solution" "ma_evidence" "{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]." "disagrees" true}] "question_id" "q-31954" "capture_key" "q-31954" "record_kind" "questions" "gap" "Correct answer does not select one typed source choice" "evidence_hash" "177d8b69c98198895c47139d66ecd90383333c6b1d4d4c48701b7551e70887e1" "final" true}}